Z||000002||JR||04-21-2001||12:49 PM||||Thanks MooCow!!<P>Yup, thats one badassed Fiero.  It.s an 88GT with 3.1 billet, polished, balance and knifedged crank.  All oiling modifications done, including 90psi oilpump.  Has SBC shaved connecting rods and Weiseco forged 11:1 pistons.  Crower highlift mechanical cam, chromemoly pushrods crane narrow roller rocker arms on 7/16 BBC posts.  Valves are titanium.  That's why it revs easily to 8000rpm!!!  Has offenhauser intake manifold ported polished heads, breathing thru Holley 490 doublepumper.  FOCA equal length headers, into 2 3/4 pipe thru cat and dual tip resonators.  Lightened flywheel and centrforce clutch.  Over a V8 car is probably some 300lbs lighter.  Ever heard an engine run 7500rpm?  Had it to 8000rpm, but it is freightening!!  This car is an adrenalin pumper.  Had it for 3 years now, drive it hard but not reckless, no problems to report.  If your ever this way e-mail me and have a look and a ride.<BR>BTW car is lowered with poly alround and engine cradle is solid mounted to frame.  Even with somewhat lumpy idle there is no harsh vibration through to thechassis.<BR>Thanks again MooCow.  Someday I'll learn how to post.<P>------------------<BR>85GT (daily driver 120,000 miles)<BR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)||||reg||6
Z||000003||TheFiero64||04-21-2001||02:35 PM||||Wow, Nice looking GT. That engine sounds like a screamer. What is that Decklid hump off of? Do you have any close-ups of it?<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
