Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||04-21-2001||07:47 PM||||This is not a flame , nor is it meant to start a war..<P>How is it 300lbs lighter than a V8 car?? Surfing the net I found most guys gain at most 190lbs over the 6<P><BR>Nice car ..you modified the decklid to fit the carb?? looks good.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000007||JR||04-22-2001||12:02 AM||||Slammed:<P>That's cool. No offense taken.  Car has no trunk, no mudguards in the wheel wells, no spare,etc.  If not 300lbs then close to it.<BR>Using MSD 6AL with spark control box in cockpit, engine produces 270HP as was built according to GM Guide to Performance Engine Building.  Engine safely revs to 7500, redlines at 8000rpm; that's why we use a lightweight valvetrain and fully balanced billet crank.<BR>Car is ferocious, but easily tamed.  Suspension mods make it very nimble, can kick the backend out predictably and gather it all back up again.  I have owned three 911's in my life, and notaone of them was as easy to drive, and this Fiero takes em, no sweat.<P>------------------<BR>85GT (daily driver 120,000 miles)<BR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)||||reg||12
Z||000008||Galen||04-22-2001||12:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jr, them got to be some fun sunday rides  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||04-22-2001||07:48 PM||||Hey JR that is a really sharp looking car. Where can I learn more about the modifications you have done? <P>I would like to know were you got the Titanium valves, valve retainers, and springs? Are the valves the stock size? What camshaft did you use? What does this thing do for performance? What do you think of those FOCOA headers? I thought the FOCOA headers were not equal length headers or did you get a custom set? Who ported the heads? Do you have any pictures of those heads for us to see? <P>If you are ever in the New England area let me know because I would definitely love to see that engine.<P>Sorry for all the questions but there are very few people here if any that have done what you have done. I am building a high performance 3.4-liter Camaro engine with many of the modifications you have done but I still want to learn more and the best information comes from the people like you who have already done it. I can never get enough information. Most people go the easy rought and swap in v8’s and other engines. I like what you have done. <P>Thanks<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||JR||04-22-2001||10:16 PM||||88formula:<P>Your right the headers are custom made here in Windsor by Fiero Conversions, said they were a copy of headers by FOCA.  Self, have never seen FOCA headers.  Cam is mechanical by Crower, high lift long duration, I beleive it is the only highperformance cam available for the 60 degree V6.  Titanium valves are from Moroso, not that much more expensive than stainless valves, size is stock.  Heads are stock but ported slightly and polished.  There is not much metal that you are able to take out of the heads so be careful.  First set of heads were ruined as tried to be too aggressive.  Bore was machined 30 over and pistons are forged Weiseco from Moroso.  BTW stainless valves are probably still able to allow you to rev to 7000rpm if you have done all the oiling mods and changed to 90psi pump.  The carb setup is crucial as tendency to overcarb.  490 is leaned out (smallest jets), but idle is still 1200rpm. Because of overlap the cam could never be used with port fuel injection.  For the power the only intake manifold available is from Offenhauser, and they will have to custom make it for you.  TransAm series in late 80's used this engine setup.  GM has carb intake manifold I believe but only for 2BBL carbs, not sure though.<BR>If you want the headers call info for Fiero Conversions in Windsor, Ontario, Canada.<BR>All info is available from HPBooks called CHEVROLET POWER: The Official Factory Performance Guide.  Must have for engine mods to do.  Any good engine shop can do the mods for you, and putting it all together is standrd procedure.  There is nothing fancy here in assembly.  Get the book. <P>------------------<BR>85GT (daily driver 120,000 miles)<BR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)||||reg||1
